From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhugengyu <zhugengyu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] mi: (dbg) Rate-limit the duplicated-frame data check

_rtw_mi_buddy_clone_bcmc_packet() compares every duplicated broadcast or
multicast frame against its copy, and a mismatch prints one warning per
frame.  Under a load that duplicates continuously this diagnostic
outruns the console: on the SDIO line it pushed the receive census and
the stall recorder's own lines out of the serial ring, so the round lost
the evidence it was collecting.

Keep the first few and every thousandth mismatch.  The path stays
visible (the counter is in the line) and the log stays usable.

Signed-off-by: zhugengyu <zhugengyu@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 core/rtw_mi.c | 17 ++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletion(-)

--- a/core/rtw_mi.c
+++ b/core/rtw_mi.c
@@ -1353,8 +1353,21 @@
 	if (_rtw_memcmp(&precvframe->u.hdr.attrib, &pcloneframe->u.hdr.attrib, sizeof(struct rx_pkt_attrib)) == _FALSE)
 		RTW_INFO("%s [WARN]  recv_frame attrib compare failed\n", __func__);
 
-	if (_rtw_memcmp(precvframe->u.hdr.rx_data, pcloneframe->u.hdr.rx_data, precvframe->u.hdr.len) == _FALSE)
-		RTW_INFO("%s [WARN]  recv_frame rx_data compare failed\n", __func__);
+	if (_rtw_memcmp(precvframe->u.hdr.rx_data, pcloneframe->u.hdr.rx_data, precvframe->u.hdr.len) == _FALSE) {
+		/*
+		 * This diagnostic fires once per duplicated frame. Under load it can
+		 * outrun the console and push the census lines out of the serial
+		 * ring, which is how a stall round loses its own evidence. Keep the
+		 * first few and every thousandth: the path is still visible, the
+		 * log is not drowned.
+		 */
+		static u32 dbg_fail_cnt;
+
+		if (dbg_fail_cnt < 5 || (dbg_fail_cnt % 1000) == 0)
+			RTW_INFO("%s [WARN]  recv_frame rx_data compare failed (n=%u)\n",
+			    __func__, dbg_fail_cnt);
+		dbg_fail_cnt++;
+	}
 
 }
 #endif
